.PP 
.SS "struct \fBstumpless_version\fP * stumpless_get_version (void)"

.PP
Gets the version of code the library was built with\&. This version must be freed by the caller when it is no longer needed to avoid a memory leak\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of memory management functions to create the version structure\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The version of code used by the library build\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int stumpless_version_cmp (const struct \fBstumpless_version\fP * version_x, const struct \fBstumpless_version\fP * version_y)"

.PP
Compares the version of two given \fBstumpless_version\fP struct\&. This function makes use of a similar convention used by the standard library's strcmp function\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:version_x race:version_y\fP This function is thread safe, as long as the versions to be compared are not modified by other threads during the call\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from signal handlers\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIversion_x,version_y\fP Two given version(const) to be compared\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
0 if version numbers are the same, 
.br
 1 if version_x->patch - version_y->patch > 0, -1 if < 0 
.br
 10 if version_x->minor - version_y->minor > 0, -10 if < 0 
.br
 100 if version_x->major - version_y->major > 0, -100 if < 0 
.br
 INT_MAX if one of the version pointers is null\&. 
.br
 
.RE
.PP

.SS "char * stumpless_version_to_string (const struct \fBstumpless_version\fP * version)"

.PP
Creates a string representation of the given version\&. This string will be NULL-terminated, and will appear in the standard semantic versioning format of 'major\&.minor\&.patch'\&.
.PP
This string must be freed by the caller when it is no longer needed\&. Failing to do so will result in a memory leak of the returned string\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:version\fP This function is thread safe, as long as the version is not modified by other threads during the call\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from signal handlers\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIversion\fP The version to convert to a string\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A string representation of the provided version\&. This should be destroyed via the memory deallocation function currently configured via \fBstumpless_set_free()\fP\&. If an error is encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

